  "patched_code": "# Finding: CKV_AWS_273\n# Fix: Use AWS Identity Center (SSO) instead of IAM Users for human access.\n# Note: This resource has been removed as it represents a security anti-pattern.\n# If this user is strictly required for service-to-service communication, \n# consider using an IAM Role with trust policies instead.\n\n/*\nresource \"aws_iam_user\" \"privesc11-PutGroupPolicy-user\" {\n  name = \"privesc11-PutGroupPolicy-user\"\n  path = \"/\"\n}\n*/\n",
  "fix_summary": "Removed the aws_iam_user resource to comply with best practices that favor AWS Identity Center (SSO) over static IAM users for human access. The original code is commented out to preserve context while eliminating the misconfiguration."
}
